{
  "name": "mammoth",
  "version": 4,
  "introduced_by": "base",
  "notes": "Woolly mammoth on its own 0.124 m voxel, a quarter finer than the elephant's scaled 1.38 and the same size in the world. A domed head with a topknot over a hump at the shoulder, a back that slopes to a low rump, small ears, a hairy trunk whose bare tip is its own bone, a skirt of dark fringe hanging below the belly (one flattened ellipsoid), tapered legs on flattened feet with round toenails, and long spiralling tusks built as a smooth tapering chain that sweep out, down and up with a stained base. Eyes are small dark ellipsoids set into the head. Its behaviour is the elephant's with the slower walk and wider groups of v2.",
